    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "at $ p_{1}=p_{2}=0.5 $, the gene frequency at which heterozygosity is most pronounced. With dominance, however, the additive genetic variance is maximized at a higher frequency of the recessive allele. This occurs because rare recessive alleles cause little genetic variance, due to their infrequent expression.",
      "source_page": 86,
      "printed_page": 66,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter4:p020:b4",
        "Genetics_chapter4:p021:b2"
      ],
